{
  "description": "Budget ledger semantics (P6.5). One table for Node (domain/budget-ledger.ts over its in-memory and Mongo stores) and Python (harness_core.budget, InMemoryBudgetLedger). Amounts are {usd, tokens} with usd in integer micro-USD; a cap dimension of null has no limit of its own (it draws from its parent), an available dimension of null is unbounded. Each scenario starts from an empty ledger at a fixed time for tenant `org-v`; steps run in order. `expect` lists only the fields checked: reserve → granted; commit/release → charged, crossed, state; remaining → available, committed, reserved, exhausted; a refusal is {\"refused\": <reason code>}. `advance` moves the clock by seconds. `pin` registers what the host pinned for a run (lazy opening). A commit's `usage` ({input, output, cacheRead, cacheWrite}, as the settler reported the call) is added to the run's own `used` with its first commit only, never to an ancestor's; remaining → used (OWD-8: the ledger is the authority on a run's usage). WP-66: a commit with `hold` ({usd, tokens}) and `holdTtlS` charges `actual` as the gateway's estimate: the call counts in remaining → estimated (on every account of the path, as committed is) and `hold` stays reserved on the path past any cap until a `reconcile` (the provider's `actual` and `usage` replace the estimate's, once; the hold goes back) or until `holdTtlS` passes, closing the run notwithstanding. A reconcile of a commit that was not estimated leaves it as it is; of a reservation never committed is refused.",
